R2338	Cueing Arg1:T2175 Arg2:T2174	
R2339	Speaker Arg1:T2176 Arg2:T2174	
T2177	Quotation 391069 391084	"And not only,"
T2178	Entity 391085 391097	the druggist
T2179	Cue 391098 391105	went on
T2180	Quotation 391107 391786	"are human beings subject to such anomalies, but animals also. Thus you are not ignorant of the singularly aphrodisiac effect produced by the Nepeta cataria, vulgarly called catmint, on the feline race; and, on the other hand, to quote an example whose authenticity I can answer for. Bridaux (one of my old comrades, at present established in the Rue Malpalu) possesses a dog that falls into convulsions as soon as you hold out a snuff-box to him. He often even makes the experiment before his friends at his summer-house at Guillaume Wood. Would anyone believe that a simple sternutation could produce such ravages on a quadrupedal organism? It is extremely curious, is it not?"
R2340	Speaker Arg1:T2178 Arg2:T2177	
R2341	Cueing Arg1:T2179 Arg2:T2177	
